# Dev tooling, never part of the mod.
#
# tests/hook_harness.lua names engine modules in string literals (it stubs
# them), which modkit's scan reports as "unresolved: engine module names
# spelled in a literal this scan cannot tie to a require".  Sixteen such
# lines would bury a real finding -- the same reason [ERRS] output is kept
# terse -- and the file does not ship: both test_build.sh and the release
# workflow exclude tests/.
#
# NOTE: modkit matches these as EXACT relative paths (`rel in ignored`,
# tools/modkit.py:189) -- NOT prefixes and NOT globs.  A bare "tests/"
# silently matches nothing, which is how this file spent its first
# revision doing exactly nothing.  Name each file.
tests/hook_harness.lua
